    "note": "STEM/learning film, hai Plain register on the ai-explainer chassis. Thesis: a percentage from a small test hides how much it could move; report a confidence interval, and for proportions near 0 or 100% use the Wilson interval, which stays inside the possible range. It measures uncertainty from sample size, not bias, and covers only the errors you planted. Worked example: Week 11's four Wilson 95% intervals. B01's 74.0% / 150 planted errors are the Week 8 test (prior week). The Your Turn example (45 of 60) is Janvi's supplied task.",
